    {
      "id": "p0102-b011",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The translator localized this wordplay by having Parsnik offer \"Hebi Star Noodles\" in Japanese. This name plays with the words hebi (\"snake\") and bebī (\"baby\") to humorously refer to Baby Star Ramen, a famous Japanese snack. Second, the noodles in Baby Star Ramen roughly look like countless baby snakes. The result is a snake-themed snack joke that parallels the original line in a uniquely Japanese way.",
        "raw": "The translator localized this wordplay\nby havingParsnik offer \"Hebi Star\nNoodles\" in Japanese. This name plays\nwith the words hebi (\"snake\") and\nbebf (\"baby\") to humorously refer to\nBaby Star Ramen, a famous Japanese\nsnack. Second, the noodles in Baby Star\nRamen roughly look like countless baby\nsnakes. The result is a snake-themed\nsnack joke that parallels the original\nline in a uniquely Japanese way.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
